and Maram (Yahya Kitana), who wrestle to hold onto their friendship in the wake of a police stop and search. As the ripples take hold, the boys try to make sense of the men they are becoming – and how letting go can be the hardest part of growing up.\\nWritten and directed by acclaimed artist Imran Perretta and co-written by Enda Walsh (Hunger), Ish was shot by cinematographer Jermaine Canute Edwards (My Father’s Shadow) and also stars singer/songwriter Joy Crookes.\",\"translations\":[]},\"shortSynopsis\":{\"text\":\"Set and filmed in Luton, Ish follows 12-year-old best friends Ish (Farhan Hasnat) and Maram (Yahya Kitana), who wrestle to hold onto their friendship in the wake \",\"translations\":[]},\"censorRatingId\":\"HO00000006\",\"censorRatingNote\":{\"text\":\"strong language\",\"translations\":[]},\"releaseDate\":\"2026-07-31\",\"runtimeInMinutes\":87,\"trailers\":[{\"provider\":\"Moviexchange\",\"uri\":\"https://film-cdn.moviexchange.com/api/cdn/release/eae7aec1-63ec-493e-9d25-91475dacb739/media/TrailerVideo\"},{\"provider\":\"External\",\"uri\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fWvNcjOGTtM\"}],\"trailerUrl\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fWvNcjOGTtM\",\"displayPriority\":10,\"castAndCrew\":[{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014160\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014161\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014162\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014163\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014164\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014165\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014166\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014167\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014168\",\"roles\":[\"Actor\"]},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014169\",\"roles\":[\"Director\"]}],\"actors\":[{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014160\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014161\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014162\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014163\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014164\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014165\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014166\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014167\"},{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014168\"}],\"directors\":[{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014169\"}],\"producers\":[],\"genreIds\":[\"0000000002\"],\"externalIds\":{\"moviexchangeReleaseId\":\"eae7aec1-63ec-493e-9d25-91475dacb739\",\"corporateId\":null},\"hopk\":\"HO00007157\",\"hoCode\":\"A000008809\",\"eventId\":null,\"distributorName\":\"BFI\"},{\"id\":\"HO00007228\",\"title\":{\"text\":\"DocHouse: The Phantom Pain of Rojava\",\"translations\":[]},\"synopsis\":{\"text\":\"In the autonomous Kurdish state of Rojava, northern Syria, a group of female fighters once dreamt of changing the world.\\n\\nIn the shadow of a failed revolution, Emmy-winning director Maryam Ebrahimi captures the hopes and dreams of these former guerrillas. Once celebrated as global heroes in the war against Islamic State, they now find themself abandoned by their allies, living secretly in a house for wounded soldiers.\\n\\nTHE PHANTOM PAIN OF ROJAVA is a post-war story, following a hidden community over the course of five years, as they struggle to rebuild their bodies and maintain their faith in the Women’s Revolution they dedicated their lives to protecting.\",\"translations\":[]},\"shortSynopsis\":null,\"censorRatingId\":\"VS00000007\",\"censorRatingNote\":null,\"releaseDate\":\"2026-07-31\",\"runtimeInMinutes\":81,\"trailers\":[],\"trailerUrl\":null,\"displayPriority\":50,\"castAndCrew\":[{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014337\",\"roles\":[\"Director\"]}],\"actors\":[],\"directors\":[{\"castAndCrewMemberId\":\"0000014337\"}],\"producers\":[],\"genreIds\":[\"0000000006\"],\"externalIds\":{\"moviexchangeReleaseId\":null,\"corporateId\":null},\"hopk\":\"HO00007228\",\"hoCode\":\"A000008894\",\"eventId\":null,\"distributorName\":\"DocHouse\"}],\"castAndCrew\":[{\"id\":\"0000014160\",\"name\":{\"givenN